    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n91026" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρωτό-πλοος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, 
			Att.
		
		
			contr.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρωτό-πλους</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ουν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>going to sea for the first time</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νηῦς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					8.35
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				1531
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. πλάτα</span> the
				<i>first-plied</i> oar (of the ship Argo), <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Andr.</u>
				865
			</span></i> (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>M.</u>
				9.32
			</span></i>: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. νεότης</span>
			<i>just embarking on the sea</i> of love, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Epigr.</u>
				30
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρωτοπόρος</span>
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>sailing first</i> or <i>foremost</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				5.1.27
			</span></i>: pr.n. of Athenian warship, H.E.K. Schmidt <i>Die Namen der
				attischen Kriegsschiffe</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				7
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(v B.C.)</span>.</div>
